---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';
---

<Base title="About">
  <h1>About</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      I'm Kyungmin Inn, a Computer Engineering student at the University of Michigan. I work on vulnerability
      research and exploitation: memory corruption in userland services, Windows kernel drivers, and embedded and
      IoT firmware. Lately that also means the physical side of it — a board on the bench, a probe on a pin, and
      what the hardware leaks while it runs.
    </p>
    <p>
      I tend to treat security as computer architecture taken one level further. Reading allocator internals or a
      speculative-execution paper is interesting to me for the same reason: it is the machine's own rules, used in a
      way nobody planned for.
    </p>

    <h2>Now</h2>
    <p>
      On leave from Michigan for independent research after military service in the Republic of Korea Army.
      Returning to Ann Arbor in January 2027.
    </p>

    <h2>Education</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>University of Michigan</strong> — B.S.E. Computer Engineering, expected May 2029.<br />
      GPA 3.96/4.00. James B. Angell Scholar, Dean's List.<br />
      <span class="muted">Coursework: Programming and Data Structures (EECS 280), Discrete Mathematics (EECS 203).</span
      >
    </p>

    <h2>Experience</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Republic of Korea Army</strong>, Daegu — Satellite Communications Operator, Oct 2024 – Apr 2026.<br />
      Recognized as an Outstanding Soldier by the company commander; completed the full term of service as Sergeant.
    </p>

    <h2>Timeline</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Period</th>
          <th scope="col">Where</th>
          <th scope="col">What</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>2026 –</td>
          <td>Independent</td>
          <td>Vulnerability research, embedded and hardware security</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>2024 – 2026</td>
          <td>Republic of Korea Army</td>
          <td>Satellite Communications Operator, Sergeant</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>2023 – 2024</td>
          <td>University of Michigan</td>
          <td>B.S.E. Computer Engineering</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>2018 – 2023</td>
          <td>Semiahmoo Secondary School, Surrey, BC</td>
          <td>High school</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>Skills</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Languages:</strong> C, C++, Python, x86 and ARM assembly</li>
      <li><strong>Systems and embedded:</strong> embedded Linux, STM32, bare metal, Keil µVision, ChipWhisperer</li>
      <li><strong>Security and analysis:</strong> Ghidra, WinDbg, GDB, QEMU; reverse engineering, binary exploitation</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <ul>
      {
        SITE.email && (
          <li>
            Email: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>
          </li>
        )
      }
      {
        SITE.github && (
          <li>
            GitHub: <a href={SITE.github}>{SITE.github.replace('https://', '')}</a>
          </li>
        )
      }
      {
        SITE.velog && (
          <li>
            Velog (Korean): <a href={SITE.velog}>{SITE.velog.replace('https://', '')}</a>
          </li>
        )
      }
    </ul>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  td:first-child {
    white-space: nowrap;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
</style>
